Exceptions are errors or problems a program encounters during execution. This either terminates
the execution of the program abruptly or give an unexpected output.

SOME EXCEPTIONS:
1. ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException: Trying to access an array position that does not exist.

2. Division by Zero: This is an ArithmeticException that displays an  error message when an attempt to
to make a Zero division in an arithmetic expression.

3. NullPointerException: When a program tries to access a method with null object.

4. InvalidInput: When a user entered a wrong input in a field. E.g. Entering a number
 instead of a string in a field. This raise an InputMismatchException.

5. FileNotFoundException: Attempting to access a file that does not exist.

6. ClassCastException: An attempt to cast an object into an incompatible data type

7.OutOfMemoryException: When the program runs out of available memory during execution.



